<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cüneyd Bey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1425</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as İzmiroğlu Cüneyd Bey</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cüneyd Bey was a Turkish lord who held Smyrna and fought to restore the Aydinid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a> in the decades after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a>'s victory over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in 1402. He changed sides repeatedly in the Ottoman civil war and later supported the pretender Düzmece Mustafa against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murad-ii">Murad II</a>. Besieged by the Ottomans, he surrendered and was executed in 1425, ending the Aydinid state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cuneyd-bey.jpg" alt="Cüneyd Bey" width="320" height="159" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anatolian_Beyliks,_Aydin._Junayd_b._Ibrahim._Second_reign,_AH_813-816_AD_1410-1413._AR_Ak%C3%A7e_(14.1mm,_0.66_g,_5h)._Without_mint-name._Undated._Near_VF.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
